# Docker build context filter for the PocketBase image (deploy/pocketbase/Dockerfile).
#
# We deploy with build context = REPO ROOT (so the Dockerfile can COPY tool/dev/pb_migrations),
# but the PocketBase image needs ONLY the migration files. Without this filter, Fly uploads the
# entire working directory (~1.4 GB: build/, .dart_tool/, etc.) on every deploy for no reason.
#
# Strategy: ignore everything, then explicitly UN-ignore what the image build needs.
# This affects ONLY the Docker build context — not git, not the Flutter/Vercel web build.

# Ignore everything by default.
*

# Un-ignore the migrations the Dockerfile copies (path must be walked from the root down).
!tool
tool/*
!tool/dev
tool/dev/*
!tool/dev/pb_migrations
!tool/dev/pb_migrations/**

# Un-ignore the Dockerfile itself (harmless, keeps the context self-describing).
!deploy
deploy/*
!deploy/pocketbase
deploy/pocketbase/*
!deploy/pocketbase/Dockerfile
